# nr-tui-surface-layout: integration fragment

Fills `mixdog_tui::surface` (panel epoch, owner and claims, Enter latch and index mode, layout signature, shell layout, panel
transition, prompt rows). Nothing in it was compiled by its author (no cargo in the task); the lead compiles it with the wave.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

The `mixdog-tui` package gains one dependency edge: `mixdog-tui-widgets` (a workspace member, already in the lock). In the
`[[package]] name = "mixdog-tui"` entry, add `"mixdog-tui-widgets",` to `dependencies` (keep the list sorted). No package is
added to the lock. `mixdog-tui/Cargo.toml` already carries the edge (`mixdog-tui-widgets = { workspace = true }`, the
workspace dependency exists).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

No change: the crate takes no external dependency it did not have.

## Protocol rows, SERVICE_PENDING, registrations

None. The surface is application state of the terminal UI; it registers no protocol method.

## Notes for the lead

* Tests: `cargo test --offline -p mixdog-tui` runs `surface_epoch` (the cases of shell-layout.test.mjs, panel-epoch.test.mjs and
  panel-handoff.test.mjs that need no picker factory) and `layout_twin` (golden `tests/goldens/layout.json`, 720 layouts, the
  row functions, the signature grammar, 60 sequences of surface operations). The recorder check is
  `node native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/recorders/record-layout.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --check native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/goldens/layout.json`
  (passed when the golden was written).
* `live-spinner-visibility.mjs` is ported by `nr-tui-widgets-status` (same wave) in
  `mixdog-tui-widgets/src/spinner.rs` (`is_live_spinner_meta_visible(&SpinnerVisibility)`,
  `is_completed_transcript_tail_appended_this_commit`). This branch was cut before that one, so it carries a private copy of
  both. When both are merged, delete the copies (one implementation; mixdog-tui already depends on mixdog-tui-widgets):
  - `mixdog-tui/src/surface/layout/budgets.rs`: delete `pub fn is_live_spinner_meta_visible(...)` and its doc comment; add
    `use mixdog_tui_widgets::spinner::{SpinnerVisibility, is_live_spinner_meta_visible};` and in `compute_row_budgets` write
    `let prompt_meta_visible = is_live_spinner_meta_visible(&SpinnerVisibility { input_box_hidden: surfaces.input_box_hidden,
    slash_palette_open: input.slash_palette_open, live_spinner: hints.live_spinner, live_spinner_is_command:
    hints.live_spinner_is_command, latest_transcript_item: hints.latest_transcript_item.as_ref().map(|item|
    mixdog_tui_widgets::spinner::TranscriptTail { kind: &item.kind, id: item.id.as_deref() }), streaming_tail:
    state.streaming_tail.as_ref().map(|tail| mixdog_tui_widgets::spinner::StreamingTail { kind: &tail.kind, streaming:
    tail.streaming, text: &tail.text }), transcript_view_active: state.transcript_view_active });`.
    In `mixdog-tui/src/surface/layout.rs` drop `is_live_spinner_meta_visible` from the `pub use budgets::{...}` list.
  - `mixdog-tui/src/surface/layout/transition.rs`: delete `fn completed_tail_appended_this_commit` and its unit test
    `only_a_done_row_appended_in_this_commit_backfills` (the widget's own tests pin it); in `same_commit_backfill_rows` call
    `mixdog_tui_widgets::spinner::is_completed_transcript_tail_appended_this_commit(latest.map(|item|
    mixdog_tui_widgets::spinner::TranscriptTail { kind: &item.kind, id: item.id.as_deref() }), previous_tail_id)`.
  The twin `layout_twin` covers both paths, so it shows a mismatch at once.
* `btw_panel_rows` (btw-controller.mjs `btwPanelRows`) lives in `surface::layout` because the row budgets need it;
  `nr-tui-panels` (which ports btw-controller.mjs) calls it instead of writing a second copy.

## Test cases not ported here (route to the picker and slash tasks)

`surface_epoch.rs` ports every case of shell-layout.test.mjs and the ownership cases of panel-epoch.test.mjs and
panel-handoff.test.mjs that need no picker factory. The cases below drive a real picker factory (none exists in Rust yet) and
no later task names them; each must become a Rust test in the task that ports that factory:
  - nr-tui-pickers-settings (settings-picker, maintenance-pickers): output-style cycle / workflow cycle preflight resolving
    after Esc does not re-open Settings; undisturbed output-style cycle still refreshes Settings; Update panel repaints its
    first check across the Settings to Update handover; Esc on the Update panel kills its in-flight first check; Esc during
    the Update panel's pending first read; Esc during a pending Settings open; an uninterrupted open still paints and keeps
    repainting; probes: Update re-check after Esc, Auto-clear read after Esc; handoff: Settings paints its loading
    destination before the daemon snapshot settles; workflow and output-style saves keep the Settings handoff visible until
    their writes settle.
  - nr-tui-pickers-extensions (extension-pickers): Esc during a pending Plugins open; late Agent "Not used" ack does not
    overwrite the replacement panel; undisturbed Agent ack still reopens Agents.
  - nr-tui-pickers-model (model-picker, route-pickers, theme-effort-pickers): model load completing after Esc paints nothing;
    Model save hands the Settings panel back on the keypress before the write settles; theme selection hands directly to
    Settings without a null panel (through the real factory); main-provider Enter still opens the provider action panel.
  - nr-tui-pickers-provider (onboarding-steps, provider-setup-picker): onboarding Step 1 does not paint when Esc lands during
    its read; empty-catalog fallback does not delegate to Providers after Esc, and an uninterrupted one still does; Step 2
    empty-model fallback does not reopen Step 1 after Esc; onboarding Web Search fallback does not jump to Step 2 after Esc.
  - nr-tui-slash (slash-dispatch): slash option entry keeps a loading panel until the async picker paints; Esc on slash
    loading prevents the pending picker from appearing later (through the real dispatch).
  - The two source audits of panel-epoch.test.mjs (raw panel sinks unreachable outside the owning layer; App.jsx routes every
    handover through shouldSupersedePanelEpoch) are enforced by the types here: the context and usage sinks are private to
    `surface::owner`, and every picker write goes through `PanelSurface::update_picker`, which applies the rule.
